<item><title>Cameroon plans CFA50 billion more in annual beverage taxes</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-plans-cfa50-billion-more-in-annual-beverage-taxes-af0d44/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-plans-cfa50-billion-more-in-annual-beverage-taxes-af0d44/</guid><category>Cameroon</category><description>The 2027 finance bill would raise excise duties and add a CFA5 stamp duty to each bottled drink.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 22:53:07 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-plans-cfa50-billion-more-in-annual-beverage-taxes-af0d44/share.jpg" length="41472" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/cameroon-plans-cfa50-billion-more-in-annual-beverage-taxes-af0d44/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>World Bank adds CFA36 billion for Cameroon rice irrigation</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/world-bank-adds-cfa36-billion-for-cameroon-rice-irrigation-bad5bb/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cm/world-bank-adds-cfa36-billion-for-cameroon-rice-irrigation-bad5bb/</guid><category>Cameroon</category><description>The extra $60 million will fund unfinished works in the Benoue Valley and extend the project deadline to June 30, 2029.</description><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 16:43:39 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cm.jpg" length="34085" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cm.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
